ess from the prior pin via gh api compare, ahead_by 3 / behind_by 0 / merge_base = old pin, per ADR-2607022900), then manually fired workflow_dispatch against both real repos and polled to completion -- https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-851/actions/runs/29652008584 and https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-6820/actions/runs/29652009332 both completed conclusion=success, every job step succeeded including each repo's own 'commit when changed' step logging 'console unchanged' (confirming CI's own independent regeneration byte-matched the merged commit -- the strongest idempotency signal, observed from live CI execution); (6) curled both live GitHub Pages URLs directly -- https://cloud-itonami.github.io/cloud-itonami-isic-851/samples/operator-console.html and https://cloud-itonami.github.io/cloud-itonami-isic-6820/samples/operator-console.html both confirmed serving the new build-time-generated content (schoolops.render-html / realty.render-html markers + real student-1/property-1 rows present). Also advanced manifest/west.yml pins for both repos via the mandatory GitHub API single-entry-commit workflow (sha-guarded PUT against the exact blob sha, commit 9fb9b892ba2e5f3fe451fca83dfad689267a9412 on com-junkawasaki/root main, verified pure forward progress via gh api compare before writing), then synced the shared orgs/ checkout via `west update --fetch smart cloud-itonami-isic-851 cloud-itonami-isic-6820` (after first repairing a shallow-graft false-positive `unrelated histories` error on the superproject's own main checkout via gh api compare confirming pure fast-forward, then `git fetch --deepen=15` + `git merge --ff-only` per CLAUDE.md's documented remedy) -- both local checkouts now match their pins with zero checkout-lag. Re-ran the fleet-wide scanner (90-docs/business/scripts/flagship-checklist-scan.cljs) over all 1,109 real checkouts to confirm the delta at fleet scale: item2-likely-generated 3->5, item4-has-regenerate-yml 1->3, item2-unknown-no-demo 930->928, checkout-lag-true unchanged at 3 (isic-6310/7810/2910, unrelated pre-existing lag from ledger seq 5, not touched this iteration) -- exactly the expected delta, confirming both the new fixes and that nothing else was inadvertently disturbed.", :event/not-done "Did not attempt the ~26-repo run-operation/build-stub sub-cluster (isic-0111/1040-style, an older non-StateGraph pattern) -- a further, smaller candidate for a SEPARATE template variant, flagged as follow-up, not attempted this iteration. Did not touch the ~290 empty/stub repos (no actor to render from at all) nor the ~456 structurally-other repos (multi-domain, HTTP-service, or other shapes) -- explicitly out of scope for this template, a separate unsolved body of work covering the majority of the fleet. Did not promote isic-851 or isic-6820 to the flagship cohort (cloud-itonami-vertical-maturity.edn) -- checklist items 1/3/5/6/7 were not evaluated this iteration, promotion is a separate, larger decision. Did not build a kotoba-ui/shitsuke.hig-integrated version of the rendered HTML -- these are standalone pure-JVM-Clojure repos with zero npm/cljs toolchain, architecturally incompatible with kotoba-ui's SSR-via-reagent-seam pipeline; followed the existing isic-2910 precedent instead (single inline <style> block, semantically-named CSS classes defined once, not scattered ad-hoc hex) and noted this tension explicitly in the template doc rather than silently glossing over it or forcing a mismatched dependency into a zero-JS repo.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607189300-cloud-itonami-flagship-wave5-all-repo-rollout-tracking", :event/seq 6, :event/at "2026-07-18T16:37:19Z"}
