EAL superproject root (/Users/junkawasaki/github/com-junkawasaki, the shared 'integration-only' checkout) since that is what all prior ledger entries mean by 'local checkouts' and since `west update` there is a read-only pin-sync operation (not a content edit/commit), explicitly distinct from the 'never commit in the shared checkout' rule. First synced the root's own tracked-file state to origin/main (fetch + ff-only merge, hit and repaired the documented shallow-graft false-positive '(forced update)'/'unrelated histories' pattern twice via `git fetch --deepen=15` after confirming via gh api compare each time that the true state was a pure fast-forward, ahead_by>0/behind_by=0 -- never trusted the local error message alone, per CLAUDE.md's explicit guidance). Checked each of the 13 for dirty/uncommitted local state BEFORE running west update (git status --short): 12 were clean; cloud-itonami-isic-6310 had a pre-existing, unrelated uncommitted change to .gitignore (adding aozora.app actor-identity ignore patterns -- not something this rollout's iterations made, evidently another parallel task's WIP sitting in the shared checkout) -- did NOT touch, discard, or force past it, per CLAUDE.md's explicit prohibition on `west update --force`/destroying WIP in a shared checkout; left it and reported it here instead. `west update` on the other 12 succeeded cleanly: isic-2910/0230/2818/6491/9522/7810 (6 repos) moved from their long-stale checkout-lag state (some dating back to before Wave5 touched them at all) to their correct, already-advanced west.yml pins; isic-851/6820/6399/5820 were already in sync (851/6820 from seq 6's own sync work, 6399 from its original pre-Wave5 state, 5820 because Wave5 has never touched it). isic-6491's update surfaced a benign `git checkout` side-effect worth recording (not a defect): 3 commits from its old detached-HEAD position were reported 'left behind, not connected to any branch' -- verified via `git cat-file -t` that these are still present as fetched objects on disk (not lost) and are unrelated content still on GitHub's own history regardless; this is expected churn from west's detached-HEAD checkout style, not data loss. AFTER the 6 new repos closed later in this same iteration, ran a SECOND `west update --fetch smart` pass for exactly those 6 (isic-0510/1622/3220/4661/750/9200), all clean/no-dirty, all succeeded -- meaning this iteration's own new closures were synced to zero checkout-lag within the same iteration, unlike seq 7 which deliberately left its 4 closures lagged. Final consolidated check across all 17 rollout-touched repos (name/pinned-revision/local-HEAD comparison, read directly off manifest/west.yml and each checkout's actual `git rev-parse HEAD`): 16/17 match exactly; the sole mismatch is cloud-itonami-isic-6310, correctly and explicitly left alone for the reason above (not a bug, not silently ignored -- the .gitignore diff was read and is reproduced in full in this ledger entry's own drafting notes for anyone who wants to reconcile it later).", :event/scanner-rerun "Re-ran 90-docs/business/scripts/flagship-checklist-scan.cljs (unmodified) over the full 1,109-repo fleet, --data-root the real superproject root (now synced), immediately after the checkout-lag remediation above so the report reflects genuinely-current on-disk state rather than stale snapshots. New aggregate vs. seq 7's last-recorded aggregate: item4-has-regenerate-yml 3 -> 15, item4-has-any-cron-workflow 3 -> 15, item2-likely-generated 5 -> 16, item2-unknown-no-demo 928 -> 918 (net -10: -6 for this iteration's new closures, -4 for the checkout-lag repos whose disk state had been silently undercounting them as 'unknown-no-demo' purely due to stale checkouts, not because they lacked generators), item6 fields unchanged (out of scope this iteration), checkout-lag-true 7 -> 1 (only isic-6310 remains, expected and explained), checkout-lag-unknown unchanged at 35 (the orphan west.yml-registration gap first flagged in seq 5, still not attempted, still a separate body of work), has-generator-missing-regenerate-workflow 2 -> 1 (the remaining 1 is isic-6310 itself -- it has always had a generator since before Wave5, and gained regenerate.yml in iteration 1, but its ON-DISK snapshot is frozen at its pre-iteration-1 state due to the unrelated dirty .gitignore blocking any further west update; GitHub-true state has both, exactly as this scanner's own :checkout/lag? mechanism is designed to explain). Wrote the refreshed report (973,375 bytes, scanned in 15,998ms) to 90-docs/business/cloud-itonami-flagship-checklist-scan.edn via the mandated single-entry sha-guarded GitHub API PUT (commit 293db425beef0f395f16d0e5108d1a10cc085e0b on com-junkawasaki/root main) -- did not hand-edit, did not touch any other file in the same commit.", :event/template-track-record "13 of the ~290-repo shape-matched cluster now closed on GitHub (cloud-itonami-isic-2910 origin pattern [seq 4, predates the formal template] + isic-851/isic-6820 [seq 6] + isic-0230/isic-2818/isic-6491/isic-9522 [seq 7] + isic-0510/isic-1622/isic-3220/isic-4661/isic-750/isic-9200 [this iteration]) -- the template has now been independently proven across 12 uses (13 counting the origin pattern) spanning forestry, manufacturing (automotive/power-tools/wood-millwork/musical-instruments), finance (leasing), education, real-estate, repair-services, mining, wholesale trade, veterinary services, and gambling/entertainment -- 10+ distinct real-world sectors, zero forced fits across the whole run, one honest evidence-backed drop (iso3166-jor, seq 7). Subject-key field variants now documented across all uses: :subject (isic-2910/6820/2818/6491/9200/4661/9522-style majority), :student-id (isic-851), :site-id (isic-0510, new this iteration). Remaining unclosed shape-matched pool: approximately 290 - 13 = 277 (mechanical estimate from the 205-candidate filtered list computed at the start of this iteration, itself already excluding the 12 closed-as-of-the